{offset200}{ia15}{arial}
{offset0}Deciphering: {arialbld}Chief Barkod{arial}

from: Markus Boggus

to: {rank} {name}









Our losses have not been in vain, the heavy water production facilities have been destroyed. Rolf Olfulsen has asked me to give you a flask containing 1cm3 of heavy water weighing 1.11g as a souvenir. Rolf says you can drink it without consequences, and without advantage either.

Hmm, there's still another detail... 

A colony of Psycho scientists was lurking in the plant's subterranean complex.  We dragged them up for questioning by our psychologist, a former student of the famous professor Zigmund Shrenk.

Our man piqued the inflated ego of these lab rats by announcing that the cargo containing THEIR heavy water had been dumped and mixed into the bottom of the Baltik regular waters annihilating THEIR work.

Sure enough, one of these lunatic geniuses, pricked into excitement, couldn't help reacting to these assertions, exclaiming triumphantly:
 
-FOOLZ! Ze kargo vas a dekoy! Ze kargo of heavy vater vas loaded on a U-boat!
Zanks to our remarkable vork ze kolossal bomb vill soon be funktional and zanks to our fantastik genius you vill all be sqvashed like tiny kokroaches.

Then with a smile our psychologist drove in the final screw:
-So this famous water bomb was only a fantasy story...

Completely agitated, this well-informed maniac provided numerous technical details to convince his interrogator, even the name of the research director who could confirm his claims:

-Go ahead, call zis number (...) ask for Professor Klaus Krank, itz he who conceived ze bomb, at ze ultra secret complex on RATMÜDE island...

This ingenious blockhead suddenly broke off, red with embarrassment, realising he'd just made a blunder.


Ratmüde Island is in the Baltik Sea a few miles from the Tekton coast. To get there we'll need to cross occupied Polnakia.

Marshall Sakharin of the New Republics of Katzar has asked to join us in Polnakia's liberation.

Finishing up on some real bad news, the Psychos have a new tank, if we can call this a tank, it looks more like a battleship on caterpillars...












{center}{device12}












{offset150}Commander Boggus of the Graff-Spitz.



